< {"method":"item/completed","params":{"item":{"type":"agentMessage","id":"e4e0e299-0af8-41cd-a6c9-d674ad24b4db","text":"Round 1 complete. Here's the summary.\n\n## Files Created (9 files, 1,313 first-party lines)\n\n| File | Lines | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| [package.json](/bench/20260516-151352-two-turn-minmount-smoke/workspace/package.json) | 13 | Scripts for `npm start` and `npm test` |\n| [server.mjs](/bench/20260516-151352-two-turn-minmount-smoke/workspace/server.mjs) | 40 | Zero-dependency Node HTTP server, binds `0.0.0.0:5173` |\n| [public/index.html](/bench/20260516-151352-two-turn-minmount-smoke/workspace/public/index.html) | 70 | HTML shell with metrics, toolbar, account list, and 3 states (loading, empty, error) |\n| [public/css/styles.css](/bench/20260516-151352-two-turn-minmount-smoke/workspace/public/css/styles.css) | 344 | Dark dashboard theme, CSS custom properties, responsive layout |\n| [public/js/data.js](/bench/20260516-151352-two-turn-minmount-smoke/workspace/public/js/data.js) | 164 | Structured data: 12 accounts, 8 renewals, 8 invoices, 10 tickets, 8 usage records, 5 incidents across 5 domains |\n| [public/js/utils.js](/bench/20260516-151352-two-turn-minmount-smoke/workspace/public/js/utils.js) | 71 | Formatting, filtering, scoring helpers |\n| [public/js/components.js](/bench/20260516-151352-two-turn-minmount-smoke/workspace/public/js/components.js) | 184 | UI rendering: metrics row, account rows, detail panels, empty/error states |\n| [public/js/app.js](/bench/20260516-151352-two-turn-minmount-smoke/workspace/public/js/app.js) | 209 | App controller: state management, event binding, filter/search/detail interactions |\n| [scripts/validate.mjs](/bench/20260516-151352-two-turn-minmount-smoke/workspace/scripts/validate.mjs) | 217 | 87 assertions across 8 phases |\n\n## Validation Results\n\n`npm test` — **87 passed, 0 failed** across these phases:\n- File inventory (9 files present)\n- package.json scripts correctness\n- Server config (0.0.0.0:5173, charset)\n- HTML structure (title, scripts, a11y, state containers)\n- Data structure (6 tables, all required fields present)\n- Business rules (minimum record counts, risk distribution, health score spread)\n- CSS (custom properties, accent colors, responsive, state styles)\n- Security (no API keys, no credential leaks)\n\n## What the Page Delivers\n\n5 coherent domains — renewals, billing, support, usage, incidents — each with structured records and risk indicators. The account list shows health scores, risk badges, domain-specific risk pills, and expandable detail panels with per-domain breakdowns. Interactions include text search, risk-level dropdown, domain filter dropdown, quick-filter chips (toggle on/off), click-to-expand detail panels, and Escape to close.\n\n## Start Commands\n\n```\nnpm start        → http://localhost:5173\nnpm test         → 87 validation checks\n```\n\n## Round 2 Suggestions\n\n- Add time-series sparklines to metrics cards (usage trend, ticket volume over time)\n- Add \"acknowledge\" or \"assign\" action buttons on tickets/incidents with state mutation\n- Add a summary/detail toggle that renders a compact table view vs. the card view\n- Persist filter state in URL query params for shareable views\n- Wire the health score bar clicks to filter by that account's domain risks","phase":"final_answer","memoryCitation":null},"threadId":"019e2fa3-65fc-7381-a85d-304bffcc8f7b","turnId":"019e2fa3-6611-75b3-a4b4-77c5da9b8a36","completedAtMs":1778916569194}}
